# Checkov Custom Policy Standards

## When to Use Custom Checks
Write custom checks when built-in checkov rules don't cover:
- Organization-specific naming standards
- Internal tag compliance requirements
- Custom network hardening rules
- Proprietary resource configurations

## Python Check Layout

```
checks/
  {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_naming.py      ← naming convention enforcement
  {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_tags.py        ← required tag enforcement
  {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_network.py     ← network hardening rules
  tests/
    test_{{COMPANY_SLUG}}_naming.py
    test_{{COMPANY_SLUG}}_tags.py
```

## Python Check Boilerplate

```python
from checkov.common.models.enums import CheckCategories, CheckResult
from checkov.terraform.checks.resource.base_resource_check import BaseResourceCheck


class Check{{CHECK_CLASS_NAME}}(BaseResourceCheck):
    def __init__(self):
        name = "{{CHECK_DESCRIPTION}}"
        id = "{{CHECK_ID}}"  # Format: CKV_{{COMPANY_SLUG_UPPER}}_NNN
        supported_resources = ["{{TERRAFORM_RESOURCE_TYPE}}"]
        categories = [CheckCategories.{{CATEGORY}}]
        super().__init__(name=name, id=id, categories=categories,
                         supported_resources=supported_resources)

    def scan_resource_conf(self, conf):
        # conf is a dict of the resource attributes
        {{CHECK_LOGIC}}
        return CheckResult.PASSED


check = Check{{CHECK_CLASS_NAME}}()
```
