## YAML Check (Lightweight Option)

```yaml
---
metadata:
  name: "{{CHECK_DESCRIPTION}}"
  id: "{{CHECK_ID}}"
  category: "GENERAL_SECURITY"
  severity: "{{SEVERITY}}"  # CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, INFO
scope:
  provider: terraform
definition:
  and:
    - cond_type: attribute
      resource_types:
        - {{TERRAFORM_RESOURCE_TYPE}}
      attribute: "{{ATTRIBUTE_PATH}}"
      operator: "{{OPERATOR}}"
      value: "{{EXPECTED_VALUE}}"
```

## Check ID Convention
`CKV_{{COMPANY_SLUG_UPPER}}_NNN` — three-digit sequential number per company namespace.
Never reuse or reassign IDs; retired checks keep their number.

## Severity Levels
| Severity | When to Use |
|----------|-------------|
| CRITICAL | Exposes data, allows privilege escalation |
| HIGH | Disables security controls, public access enabled |
| MEDIUM | Missing best-practice config, weak defaults |
| LOW | Cosmetic / minor compliance issues |
| INFO | Informational — no blocking |

## Running Checks
```bash
# Run all checks including custom
checkov -d . --external-checks-dir ./checks

# Run with specific framework
checkov -d . --framework terraform --external-checks-dir ./checks

# Run only custom checks
checkov -d . --external-checks-dir ./checks --check CKV_{{COMPANY_SLUG_UPPER}}
```

## Testing Custom Checks

```python
import unittest
from checkov.runner_filter import RunnerFilter
from checkov.terraform.runner import Runner


class TestCheck{{CHECK_CLASS_NAME}}(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_pass(self):
        runner = Runner()
        results = runner.run(root_folder="./test_fixtures/pass",
                             runner_filter=RunnerFilter(checks=["{{CHECK_ID}}"]))
        self.assertEqual(len(results.failed_checks), 0)

    def test_fail(self):
        runner = Runner()
        results = runner.run(root_folder="./test_fixtures/fail",
                             runner_filter=RunnerFilter(checks=["{{CHECK_ID}}"]))
        self.assertGreater(len(results.failed_checks), 0)
```
